1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,672
Narrator: Scenario 33. Cloud platforms, containers, and automation.

2
00:00:07,272 --> 00:00:17,832
B: The new pods keep restarting with CrashLoopBackOff. Is the Kubernetes cluster unstable, or did the deployment introduce a problem with our application?

3
00:00:18,432 --> 00:00:29,472
A: Other workloads on the same nodes are stable. These containers exit within three seconds, and their last logs report a missing required configuration value.

4
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:40,440
B: Please share the previous container logs and exit code. The live logs disappear too quickly, and I want to compare them with the startup changes.

5
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:51,192
A: I attached sanitized previous logs and the deployment revision to the incident. The exit code is one, and there is no recorded memory kill.

6
00:00:51,792 --> 00:01:03,384
B: The new version requires a queue endpoint variable. It exists in staging, but the production deployment template does not reference the corresponding configuration key.

7
00:01:03,984 --> 00:01:14,160
A: That matches the error, but let us verify the intended production endpoint before adding it. We should not copy staging values into production.

8
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:26,376
B: The application configuration owner confirms the approved endpoint. I can update the template and run validation to check that every required startup value is present.

9
00:01:26,976 --> 00:01:37,128
A: How is customer traffic affected right now? The old replicas are still running, so we need their capacity and error rates before choosing the next step.

10
00:01:37,728 --> 00:01:48,480
B: The rollout stopped after two new pods failed. The old replicas retain full serving capacity, and we have not observed an increase in customer errors.

11
00:01:49,080 --> 00:02:01,488
A: Keep the rollout paused while the template correction is reviewed. After approval, validate one new pod’s startup, readiness, queue access, and a representative business transaction.

12
00:02:02,088 --> 00:02:13,512
B: I will own the correction and provide the test evidence at 14:00 UTC. If validation fails, we will stop and retain the currently serving revision.

13
00:02:14,112 --> 00:02:24,696
A: I will monitor the remaining rollout and record the configuration gap. We should add a required-value check to deployment validation before the next release.
